leyer","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_11065","person_slug":"vanessa-bleyer","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Varun Ghosh","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11017","person_slug":"varun-ghosh","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Documents — Middle East","noes":20,"question":"Lidia Thorpe I seek leave to table a document. Leave not granted. Pursuant to contingent notice standing in my name, I move: That so much of the standing orders be suspended as would prevent me tabling the document. I sought leave here today to table a document that lists the names of 21,637 children killed in Gaza between October 2023 and May 2026. The coalition does not want me to table this, and now the government don't want me to table— Penny Wong We gave leave! Lidia Thorpe Okay, I'll take that back. Thank you. These children have had their— Penny Wong Seriously. Lidia Thorpe Calm down—lives taken through a cruel genocide. Sue Lines Senator Thorpe, I'm going to remind you, as I do for all senators—you've sought to suspend because leave was denied for you to table a document. What you really need to focus on is the suspension not the substantive matter of the document you're seeking to table. You can refer to the document, but the substantive part of your five minutes needs to focus on the suspension. Lidia Thorpe These children have had their lives taken through a cruel genocide. They cannot have their identity taken away as well. They deserve to have their names heard. Their families deserve to have them remembered. This is why I'm bringing their names to the Senate today. Just last week, I was handed this box with 21,000 children's names. Sue Lines Senator Thorpe, I am going to again remind you that this is a suspension debate. Your comments need to substantially relate to the suspension. Lidia Thorpe The 21,000 names I was given in those bits of paper are in this document that I'm trying to table into the Senate. Each one contains the name of a child that was killed. I would have liked to present every single one here individually, but this place cannot deal with that. Here I am, presenting 451 densely filled pages containing the names of 21,637 children killed in Gaza. These were lives taken prematurely. These children had their— Sue Lines Senator Thorpe, I","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-10790","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2026-09-16/2"}
